{
  "id": "cumbia_peruvian",
  "name": "Cumbia peruana (chicha)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Peruvian Amazonian-and-coastal cumbia hybrid 1960s-onward, evolved from Colombian-cumbia-mainstream into a distinct fuzz-electric-guitar-led psychedelic-rock-fused subform centered in Lima, Iquitos, and Chiclayo. Built on Colombian-cumbia 4-beat-clave rhythmic-foundation but substituting electric-guitar (often with fuzz, wah, reverb, surf-twang) and electric-bass for the original gaitas-and-acoustic-bass. The chicha-cumbia 1965-1975-era originated in Andean-migrant Lima working-class-barrios and fused Andean huayno-pentatonic melodic-vocabulary with cumbia-rhythm and Anglo-American garage-and-psychedelic guitar-aesthetics. The 1970s-cumbia-amazonica branch (Iquitos-and-Pucallpa Amazon-basin) added more Afro-Caribbean and Brazilian-Northeastern-forró rhythmic-elements. 2000s-onward international-rediscovery via reissue-labels.",
